1
00:00:00,440 --> 00:00:01,810
(All character, place, group, and
institution names are fictitious.)

2
00:00:01,870 --> 00:00:03,240
(Broadcast guidelines for filming
children and teens were followed.)

3
00:00:05,310 --> 00:00:06,750
(Episode 7)

4
00:00:08,550 --> 00:00:11,220
Mom, if you fall,
your joints will give out.

5
00:00:11,280 --> 00:00:14,420
- I told you not to chase me.
- You're all so pathetic.

6
00:00:14,490 --> 00:00:17,260
You get older, you eat every meal,
and this is how you act.

7
00:00:17,320 --> 00:00:18,760
Aren't you going
to stop right there?

8
00:00:18,820 --> 00:00:20,560
You guys deserve
to be beaten to death by me,

9
00:00:20,630 --> 00:00:21,630
you punks.

10
00:00:23,560 --> 00:00:24,560
Seriously, darn it...

11
00:00:28,030 --> 00:00:29,130
Didn't you say Mi Mi
was a literary girl...

12
00:00:29,200 --> 00:00:31,070
back in the day?

13
00:00:31,140 --> 00:00:32,440
Were you a track star or something?

14
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:33,740
Wait until you get stabbed
in the back...

15
00:00:33,810 --> 00:00:34,810
by someone you trust, you punk.

16
00:00:34,870 --> 00:00:36,880
I thought you were
doing well for yourself,

17
00:00:36,940 --> 00:00:38,180
so I trusted you and left you alone.

18
00:00:38,240 --> 00:00:40,510
And you stab your mom
in the back like this?

19
00:00:43,620 --> 00:00:46,520
Oh, it's just this once.
I studied my butt off...

20
00:00:46,580 --> 00:00:48,290
and went to a top university
like you wanted,

21
00:00:48,350 --> 00:00:50,820
got a job at a big company,
and made good money.

22
00:00:50,890 --> 00:00:54,960
Have I ever upset you
with anything else until now?

23
00:00:55,030 --> 00:00:58,160
Right.
You sure have a way with words.

24
00:00:59,230 --> 00:01:02,900
I was so grateful and proud that you
studied well and worked hard,

25
00:01:02,970 --> 00:01:05,940
so out of my three kids,
I cared for you the most...

26
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:07,770
and trusted you the most.

27
00:01:07,840 --> 00:01:10,280
That's why I ignored
your grandma's objections...

28
00:01:10,340 --> 00:01:13,110
and even got you that apartment.
But you blew that house...

29
00:01:13,180 --> 00:01:15,450
and you've been hiding it
and running away?

30
00:01:15,510 --> 00:01:16,610
Are you even a man?

31
00:01:18,050 --> 00:01:20,150
Where did you sell off your balls?

32
00:01:20,220 --> 00:01:24,260
Wow, Mom, your amazing second son,
honestly, really. What?

33
00:01:25,690 --> 00:01:28,730
I definitely didn't sell them off.
And Mom,

34
00:01:28,790 --> 00:01:31,330
do you know you're scarier right now
than my senior officer in the army?

35
00:01:34,330 --> 00:01:35,430
This guy, until the very end...

36
00:01:36,800 --> 00:01:38,140
Oh, my.

37
00:01:39,770 --> 00:01:41,240
Mom.

38
00:01:41,310 --> 00:01:42,840
Oh, my.

39
00:01:42,910 --> 00:01:44,440
- Mom.
- Oh, I'm dying.

40
00:01:44,510 --> 00:01:46,010
Mom.

41
00:01:46,040 --> 00:01:47,850
Oh, my, I'm dying.

42
00:01:47,910 --> 00:01:49,850
- Mom. Are you okay?
- Oh, my, Mother.

43
00:01:49,910 --> 00:01:51,420
I can't live like this, seriously.

44
00:01:51,480 --> 00:01:54,650
- Easy...
- I told you not to chase me.

45
00:01:55,650 --> 00:01:57,760
- Oh, my.
- Get up.

46
00:01:59,820 --> 00:02:01,630
- Hey, the brush.
- What?

47
00:02:01,690 --> 00:02:03,530
- The brush, the brush.
- Forget it. Just throw this away.

48
00:02:03,600 --> 00:02:04,830
The brush, you punk.

49
00:02:05,900 --> 00:02:07,800
Oh, my. Oh, my.

50
00:02:07,870 --> 00:02:09,770
- Seriously...
- Oh, my.

51
00:02:09,830 --> 00:02:11,440
Careful.

52
00:02:11,500 --> 00:02:13,200
- Oh, my.
- Gosh.

53
00:02:13,240 --> 00:02:15,040
I told you we should go
to the hospital, Mom.

54
00:02:16,270 --> 00:02:17,840
How much could it even cost,
bringing it all the way here...

55
00:02:17,910 --> 00:02:19,810
in this situation?

56
00:02:19,880 --> 00:02:21,880
Just open the gate.

57
00:02:21,950 --> 00:02:24,420
Oh, it's open. Mom, careful.

58
00:02:25,620 --> 00:02:27,250
- Oh, my.
- Oh, my.

59
00:02:27,320 --> 00:02:28,320
Watch the step. Yes.

60
00:02:28,390 --> 00:02:31,060
Oh, my.

61
00:02:31,120 --> 00:02:32,120
Oh, my.

62
00:02:37,760 --> 00:02:40,060
What? Mom!

63
00:02:43,170 --> 00:02:45,800
Go inside quietly. Hurry.

64
00:02:45,870 --> 00:02:47,810
Wow.

65
00:02:47,870 --> 00:02:50,840
Mom, so this whole time,
you were acting?

66
00:02:50,910 --> 00:02:53,780
- To catch me?
- That is right, you punk.

67
00:02:53,850 --> 00:02:55,650
Did you think I was
just an innocent girl?

68
00:02:55,710 --> 00:02:58,750
I was in the drama club
in middle school.

69
00:02:58,820 --> 00:03:00,890
Because I met your father early
and had you kids,

70
00:03:00,950 --> 00:03:02,120
I have been working
my fingers to the bone...

71
00:03:02,190 --> 00:03:03,860
until this age.

72
00:03:03,920 --> 00:03:05,460
There was a time when I lived
exactly how I wanted,

73
00:03:05,520 --> 00:03:08,230
having the time of my life,
and doing whatever I pleased.

74
00:03:09,290 --> 00:03:13,830
Mom, but since Gang Nam got divorced
and moved back in,

75
00:03:14,930 --> 00:03:17,400
is there really a need
to tell Grandma...

76
00:03:17,470 --> 00:03:19,600
about my financial accident
right now?

77
00:03:19,670 --> 00:03:23,980
I am just worried about
Grandma's health.

78
00:03:24,040 --> 00:03:26,340
I will take care of that.

79
00:03:26,410 --> 00:03:28,180
I dragged you here because
I thought you would cause trouble...

80
00:03:28,250 --> 00:03:29,780
if I left you alone.

81
00:03:29,850 --> 00:03:30,880
Hurry up, are you not going in?

82
00:03:32,650 --> 00:03:33,650
Yes.

83
00:03:34,720 --> 00:03:35,720
I am going in.

84
00:04:10,120 --> 00:04:12,990
Unbelievable.
I was just scrubbing toilets.

85
00:04:28,210 --> 00:04:29,310
They say a woman
with no luck in men...

86
00:04:29,370 --> 00:04:31,480
has no luck with children either.

87
00:04:31,540 --> 00:04:33,040
Do they think their mother
is made of money?

88
00:04:34,580 --> 00:04:37,120
Both of my sons are
slapping me from both sides.

89
00:05:00,300 --> 00:05:01,310
Hey.

90
00:05:02,140 --> 00:05:07,110
- Oh, my. When did you get here?
- Oh, Aunt. Are you not asleep yet?

91
00:05:08,210 --> 00:05:10,250
Gosh, I cannot sleep
until your mom gets home.

92
00:05:11,880 --> 00:05:13,550
I came with Mom.

93
00:05:13,620 --> 00:05:15,890
Oh, did she go to the restaurant?

94
00:05:15,950 --> 00:05:19,160
Hey, have you still
not eaten dinner?

95
00:05:19,220 --> 00:05:21,030
Here, boil this and eat. Okay?
I will go check on her.

96
00:05:21,090 --> 00:05:22,090
Goodness.

97
00:05:23,330 --> 00:05:24,600
Oh, my.

98
00:05:24,660 --> 00:05:27,330
What is the point of being a manager
at a large company?

99
00:05:27,400 --> 00:05:30,130
We all earn money
just to eat and live, right?

100
00:05:30,200 --> 00:05:32,000
You are working so hard,
our Dae Chi. Oh, my.

101
00:05:33,340 --> 00:05:36,670
Oh, and I told your mom...

102
00:05:36,740 --> 00:05:39,580
to look at you and find
the strength to keep going.

103
00:05:39,640 --> 00:05:41,450
You are not just any ordinary son,
are you?

104
00:05:41,510 --> 00:05:44,120
You have the best education and work
for the best company in Korea.

105
00:05:45,620 --> 00:05:47,590
Just keep doing what you are doing.

106
00:05:47,650 --> 00:05:48,750
Such a good kid.

107
00:05:54,760 --> 00:05:56,690
Who is here?

108
00:05:56,760 --> 00:05:59,100
Oh, Mrs. Choi.

109
00:05:59,160 --> 00:06:01,330
Are you still awake?

110
00:06:01,400 --> 00:06:05,740
When you get closer to the grave,
your sleep gets lighter.

111
00:06:05,800 --> 00:06:07,140
Dae Chi is here.

112
00:06:07,210 --> 00:06:09,870
He said he came with Mi Mi,
but she has not come in.

113
00:06:09,940 --> 00:06:11,140
She is probably at the restaurant.

114
00:06:12,980 --> 00:06:15,910
She must have come back empty-handed
without finding Mi Seon.

115
00:06:17,650 --> 00:06:19,650
She must be heartbroken.

116
00:06:28,690 --> 00:06:31,700
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

117
00:06:35,570 --> 00:06:38,040
You already drank four glasses?

118
00:06:38,100 --> 00:06:42,840
Oh, my. Our father is going to
jump right out of his grave again.

119
00:06:42,910 --> 00:06:44,780
Gosh.

120
00:06:44,840 --> 00:06:47,410
I told you to fix this habit.

121
00:06:47,480 --> 00:06:50,180
It tastes better
when I drink it like this.

122
00:06:50,250 --> 00:06:51,950
If you sit here acting all pathetic?

123
00:06:52,020 --> 00:06:53,990
Will gold and silver
just fall from the sky?

124
00:06:54,050 --> 00:06:56,250
Of course not.

125
00:06:56,320 --> 00:06:57,490
Goodness, really.

126
00:06:58,920 --> 00:06:59,920
Here.

127
00:07:03,930 --> 00:07:07,030
Mi Seon, Su Ah's mom.

128
00:07:08,570 --> 00:07:10,670
Until she shows up
on her own two feet,

129
00:07:10,740 --> 00:07:11,970
give up on trying to find her.

130
00:07:14,640 --> 00:07:18,380
She is my child, too.
How could I do that?

131
00:07:18,440 --> 00:07:20,850
Did you not hear what Mother said?

132
00:07:20,910 --> 00:07:23,780
Come on, have we only known her
for a day or two?

133
00:07:25,020 --> 00:07:28,320
When Gang Nam first brought her
over to introduce her,

134
00:07:28,390 --> 00:07:31,590
you and me, right?
And even Mrs. Choi.

135
00:07:31,660 --> 00:07:32,860
Remember how hesitant...

136
00:07:32,920 --> 00:07:36,690
- we all were about her?
- That is why I cannot let her go.

137
00:07:36,760 --> 00:07:39,230
Because I wronged her so much.

138
00:07:41,130 --> 00:07:42,970
True.

139
00:07:43,030 --> 00:07:48,110
Just because she was an orphan
with no siblings, we really...

140
00:07:48,170 --> 00:07:49,970
Right up until
they walked down the aisle,

141
00:07:50,040 --> 00:07:53,280
we held onto Gang Nam
and tried to stop him.

142
00:07:53,340 --> 00:07:56,850
But you really have to
get to know a person. Right?

143
00:07:56,910 --> 00:07:58,150
Even if we wanted to find a flaw,

144
00:07:58,220 --> 00:07:59,550
there was absolutely nothing
to criticize. Right?

145
00:08:01,320 --> 00:08:05,020
Every time Gang Nam
ruined his business,

146
00:08:06,120 --> 00:08:08,530
she quietly worked
part-time jobs all night...

147
00:08:08,590 --> 00:08:11,000
just to earn their living expenses.

148
00:08:11,060 --> 00:08:12,330
Listen,

149
00:08:12,400 --> 00:08:14,170
when a girl like that
decides to get a divorce...

150
00:08:14,230 --> 00:08:15,830
without discussing it
with us at all...

151
00:08:15,900 --> 00:08:17,740
It means she endured
as much as she could.

152
00:08:18,940 --> 00:08:20,870
She really did endure it
for a long time.

153
00:08:23,340 --> 00:08:26,810
But is there really
no hope left for them?

154
00:08:26,880 --> 00:08:29,050
None. I am telling you to give up.

155
00:08:29,110 --> 00:08:31,880
People like her
are the scariest in the world.

156
00:08:31,950 --> 00:08:33,920
She has made up her mind
to never look back.

157
00:08:35,820 --> 00:08:38,460
Still, I feel so hurt.

158
00:08:38,520 --> 00:08:40,260
I never thought of her...

159
00:08:40,320 --> 00:08:44,760
as just a daughter-in-law.
Woman to woman, human to human,

160
00:08:44,830 --> 00:08:46,830
I could have listened
to whatever she had to say.

161
00:08:49,130 --> 00:08:50,770
She should have at least
said something before leaving.

162
00:08:50,840 --> 00:08:52,400
Gosh...

163
00:08:52,470 --> 00:08:54,440
Even Mom would kick her coffin
open and wake up.

164
00:08:54,510 --> 00:08:55,940
You do not even know
how to appreciate alcohol.

165
00:09:00,880 --> 00:09:01,950
What was Dae Chi doing?

166
00:09:03,210 --> 00:09:04,550
Probably making instant noodles?

167
00:09:07,350 --> 00:09:09,150
You lost all your energy
looking for Su Ah's mom,

168
00:09:09,220 --> 00:09:10,820
so you went to see
your precious son.

169
00:09:11,890 --> 00:09:13,460
Precious son?

170
00:09:13,520 --> 00:09:17,030
He seemed to feel a bit sorry
for missing your birthday, at least.

171
00:09:18,930 --> 00:09:21,700
Does Dae Chi know what happened
to his brother's family?

172
00:09:25,640 --> 00:09:27,140
That jerk.

173
00:09:27,240 --> 00:09:29,370
That jerk? Who?

174
00:09:30,710 --> 00:09:31,710
Gang Nam?

175
00:09:32,740 --> 00:09:34,550
Or Kang Hak Sung?

176
00:09:36,310 --> 00:09:39,050
I have no energy.
Do not ask me anymore.

177
00:09:39,120 --> 00:09:41,790
Well, I just think he is admirable.

178
00:09:41,850 --> 00:09:44,990
They say daughters are the ones who
treat you well these days,

179
00:09:45,060 --> 00:09:46,160
but honestly,

180
00:09:46,220 --> 00:09:47,460
I think a successful son
like Dae Chi...

181
00:09:47,530 --> 00:09:49,090
would be much more reliable.

182
00:09:49,160 --> 00:09:51,830
Once Da Mi gets married
and starts her own family,

183
00:09:51,900 --> 00:09:55,200
how much more could she possibly
do for you here?

184
00:09:55,270 --> 00:09:58,370
Besides, she is not even
your biological child.

185
00:09:58,440 --> 00:10:00,600
I am seriously going to sew
that mouth of yours shut...

186
00:10:00,670 --> 00:10:02,170
one of these days, very soon.

187
00:10:03,840 --> 00:10:06,440
You do not say things like that
in front of Da Mi, do you?

188
00:10:07,780 --> 00:10:08,780
What?

189
00:10:09,780 --> 00:10:12,180
Oh, no.

190
00:10:12,250 --> 00:10:17,390
Well, sometimes,
whenever that girl acts cheeky,

191
00:10:17,460 --> 00:10:19,420
I do say things
to put her in her place.

192
00:10:19,490 --> 00:10:21,690
As her aunt, you know.

193
00:10:21,760 --> 00:10:24,130
Think of it as affectionate nagging.

194
00:10:28,070 --> 00:10:30,130
How should I tell Mother?

195
00:10:39,910 --> 00:10:43,150
So, does that mean
he has no interest in you at all?

196
00:10:43,210 --> 00:10:44,720
That could be it.

197
00:10:44,780 --> 00:10:47,180
Or he could just be pretending.

198
00:10:47,250 --> 00:10:49,290
Right, it must be the latter.

199
00:10:49,350 --> 00:10:51,720
Since he is the CEO's son
and your boss,

200
00:10:51,790 --> 00:10:53,420
even if he does have
feelings for you,

201
00:10:53,490 --> 00:10:55,690
he probably cannot
show it easily, right?

202
00:10:55,760 --> 00:10:57,600
I have caught the CEO Jeon's eye,

203
00:10:57,660 --> 00:10:59,260
and his father seemed
to like me too.

204
00:11:00,500 --> 00:11:02,330
That was the vibe yesterday, Mom.

205
00:11:02,400 --> 00:11:05,540
Now, all I need to do
is win Cha Do Yun's heart.

206
00:11:05,600 --> 00:11:07,440
Oh, my baby.

207
00:11:07,510 --> 00:11:09,370
There is nothing
my daughter cannot do.

208
00:11:09,440 --> 00:11:11,880
You have always achieved
whatever you set your mind to.

209
00:11:13,440 --> 00:11:15,110
You are the only reason I live.

210
00:11:16,510 --> 00:11:19,750
Still, you should look elsewhere
from time to time, Mom.

211
00:11:19,820 --> 00:11:21,050
Where?

212
00:11:21,150 --> 00:11:22,590
I am going to be late.
I will get going.

213
00:11:22,650 --> 00:11:23,650
Oh, okay, sure.

214
00:11:24,760 --> 00:11:27,120
Ye Ri, do you want me
to give you a ride?

215
00:11:27,190 --> 00:11:28,990
The subway is faster at this hour.

216
00:11:29,060 --> 00:11:31,000
Oh, when are we moving?

217
00:11:31,060 --> 00:11:32,300
We are doing it
over the weekend, right?

218
00:11:32,360 --> 00:11:35,400
We will do it on a weekday.
We have to save every penny we can.

219
00:11:35,470 --> 00:11:37,540
Do not worry about it
at all, sweetie.

220
00:11:37,600 --> 00:11:39,700
We are hiring
full-service movers anyway.

221
00:11:39,770 --> 00:11:42,770
Our Assistant Manager Kang Ye Ri
should just hurry to work.

222
00:11:42,840 --> 00:11:44,180
- I got it.
- Have a good day.

223
00:11:44,240 --> 00:11:46,380
- Yes, I will get going.
- Have a good day, sweetie.

224
00:11:46,440 --> 00:11:48,380
- Do not come out, Mom.
- What about food?

225
00:11:48,450 --> 00:11:50,150
Didn't you cook today either?

226
00:11:50,210 --> 00:11:53,250
Well, Ye Ri said
she wanted a sandwich.

227
00:11:53,320 --> 00:11:55,050
There should be some
instant rice somewhere. Look for it.

228
00:11:56,050 --> 00:11:58,660
Come on, you should at least
make some rice, right?

229
00:11:58,720 --> 00:12:01,530
We have rice.
Is that expensive rice cooker...

230
00:12:01,590 --> 00:12:06,000
- just for decoration?
- Enough about the rice.

231
00:12:06,060 --> 00:12:07,060
Honey.

232
00:12:07,130 --> 00:12:10,400
I read somewhere that capable men
who make good money...

233
00:12:10,470 --> 00:12:13,300
do not nag their wives about food.

234
00:12:13,340 --> 00:12:15,710
- Who says that?
- On TV shows.

235
00:12:15,770 --> 00:12:17,440
There must be
real-life cases like that,

236
00:12:17,510 --> 00:12:18,710
which is why they put it in shows.

237
00:12:20,040 --> 00:12:22,910
Let's just drop it, okay?

238
00:12:27,990 --> 00:12:30,690
All this talk about
the CEO of Ye Ri's company.

239
00:12:30,750 --> 00:12:33,120
I really cannot stand
listening to it, you know?

240
00:12:35,230 --> 00:12:37,090
Do not even think about
forcing a connection...

241
00:12:37,160 --> 00:12:40,800
based on family background and money
just to get her married, okay?

242
00:12:40,870 --> 00:12:43,470
Tell Ye Ri the same thing, got it?

243
00:12:43,530 --> 00:12:44,700
What?

244
00:12:44,770 --> 00:12:47,400
Now all she needs to do
is win his heart?

245
00:12:47,470 --> 00:12:48,510
Unbelievable.

246
00:12:50,310 --> 00:12:51,410
This darn apartment.

247
00:12:51,480 --> 00:12:53,380
The soundproofing is
absolutely terrible, anyway.

248
00:12:54,910 --> 00:12:58,450
Meeting someone you connect with,
meeting your soulmate,

249
00:12:58,520 --> 00:13:00,520
should be as natural
as water flowing.

250
00:13:00,580 --> 00:13:01,920
Are you running
a sales pitch right now?

251
00:13:03,050 --> 00:13:05,990
- I am a snob.
- You were not like this at first.

252
00:13:06,060 --> 00:13:07,730
You have changed.

253
00:13:07,790 --> 00:13:10,360
Because we had nothing
from the start back then.

254
00:13:10,430 --> 00:13:13,300
Living comfortably thanks to you,
without lacking anything,

255
00:13:13,360 --> 00:13:14,930
I cannot stand hitting rock bottom.

256
00:13:16,370 --> 00:13:18,940
Honestly, just looking at the back
of your head makes me angry.

257
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:20,470
It gets on my nerves.

258
00:13:20,570 --> 00:13:23,140
So what if I am a snob?
Why? Am I the bad guy?

259
00:13:23,210 --> 00:13:26,710
Then just keep taking it out on me
and resenting me.

260
00:13:26,780 --> 00:13:29,210
Meals? I will make my own food
from now on.

261
00:13:29,280 --> 00:13:32,050
But do not do this to Ye Ri.

262
00:13:32,120 --> 00:13:34,050
I am saying this because
I am genuinely worried,

263
00:13:34,120 --> 00:13:36,920
so do not just ignore it.
I am begging you.

264
00:13:38,790 --> 00:13:39,790
I am heading out.

265
00:13:41,760 --> 00:13:42,790
Look at the great teacher.

266
00:13:44,030 --> 00:13:46,200
Anyone listening
would think he has lived...

267
00:13:46,260 --> 00:13:47,430
a picture-perfect life.

268
00:13:48,470 --> 00:13:49,500
We are both exactly the same.

269
00:13:58,810 --> 00:14:03,150
Our Seung Yun will be back soon.

270
00:14:03,210 --> 00:14:06,580
You all missed him a lot too, right?

271
00:14:12,760 --> 00:14:13,760
Mother.

272
00:14:15,790 --> 00:14:17,530
We are heading to work.

273
00:14:17,600 --> 00:14:18,830
What were you doing, Mother...

274
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:26,770
Mother, is there anything
you would like to eat?

275
00:14:26,870 --> 00:14:28,910
I will buy it on my way home.

276
00:14:28,970 --> 00:14:32,540
Never mind.
Just go out and work hard.

277
00:14:35,050 --> 00:14:37,210
Yes, we will be on our way.

278
00:14:38,450 --> 00:14:41,150
Then have a peaceful day, Mother.

279
00:14:50,130 --> 00:14:51,700
How can a mother
who outlived her child...

280
00:14:52,760 --> 00:14:55,670
have the nerve
to spend a peaceful day?

281
00:15:05,940 --> 00:15:08,250
Oh, my eyes.

282
00:15:08,310 --> 00:15:10,150
What terrible luck
first thing in the morning.

283
00:15:10,210 --> 00:15:12,050
What are you going to do, you idiot.

284
00:15:12,150 --> 00:15:13,880
Who are you blaming?

285
00:15:13,950 --> 00:15:16,790
Hey, do you not have
any basic manners?

286
00:15:16,850 --> 00:15:18,360
Do you not know how to knock?

287
00:15:19,490 --> 00:15:22,130
Did you think I knew you were home?

288
00:15:22,190 --> 00:15:24,030
When did you even
crawl back in here?

289
00:15:24,090 --> 00:15:26,960
I let you get away with everything
because you are the youngest.

290
00:15:27,030 --> 00:15:29,300
Hey, who are you calling "you?"

291
00:15:29,370 --> 00:15:30,370
Oh, I do not know,
take responsibility.

292
00:15:30,430 --> 00:15:31,500
Because of you, I am going to get...

293
00:15:31,570 --> 00:15:34,240
- complaints all day today.
- Kang Da Mi.

294
00:15:34,310 --> 00:15:36,010
That is all just superstition, kid.

295
00:15:38,710 --> 00:15:40,810
It is a kind of self-hypnosis.

296
00:15:42,280 --> 00:15:44,450
Acting all high and mighty
while sitting on a mountain of debt.

297
00:15:52,520 --> 00:15:54,760
Why are you yelling so much
this early in the morning?

298
00:15:57,290 --> 00:15:58,360
Why is Dae Chi here?

299
00:16:02,930 --> 00:16:04,470
Mom, by any chance...

300
00:16:07,200 --> 00:16:08,970
I guess you know too?

301
00:16:09,040 --> 00:16:11,810
Well, the exact details...

302
00:16:11,880 --> 00:16:14,040
I was so shocked too.

303
00:16:14,110 --> 00:16:17,150
I cut him off because
I did not want to hear any more,

304
00:16:17,210 --> 00:16:20,120
but he suddenly called me last night
offering to buy me dinner.

305
00:16:24,420 --> 00:16:26,720
He asked to borrow money.

306
00:16:29,660 --> 00:16:30,660
How much?

307
00:16:32,330 --> 00:16:33,460
Two hundred thousand dollars.

308
00:16:34,900 --> 00:16:37,100
He must be really desperate.

309
00:16:37,170 --> 00:16:41,110
- A guy with that much pride.
- Mom, but how did you know?

310
00:16:41,170 --> 00:16:43,010
There is no way
he would have confessed first.

311
00:16:44,710 --> 00:16:46,810
Do not say a word to the family.

312
00:16:46,880 --> 00:16:48,180
I am thinking about it.

313
00:16:50,180 --> 00:16:51,280
Okay.

314
00:17:05,630 --> 00:17:08,170
- Yes.
- Did you sleep well, Grandma?

315
00:17:08,230 --> 00:17:09,230
I did.

316
00:17:10,770 --> 00:17:12,600
Our Su Ah is so pretty.

317
00:17:12,670 --> 00:17:15,910
Her skills are the best, right?

318
00:17:15,970 --> 00:17:18,340
Hey, you.

319
00:17:18,410 --> 00:17:20,880
You should take care of
your mom's feelings first.

320
00:17:20,940 --> 00:17:24,150
- What?
- Spend some money this time.

321
00:17:24,210 --> 00:17:25,280
What is the point
of having a daughter...

322
00:17:25,350 --> 00:17:26,950
who works at a department store's
luxury boutique?

323
00:17:27,020 --> 00:17:29,290
Take this chance
to buy a designer scarf...

324
00:17:29,350 --> 00:17:31,050
and give it to her.

325
00:17:34,060 --> 00:17:36,590
Do not treat other people's money
so lightly.

326
00:17:36,660 --> 00:17:38,360
It is money she earns
by standing all day...

327
00:17:38,430 --> 00:17:39,830
until her body aches.

328
00:17:41,770 --> 00:17:45,240
The situation is different
this time, Mrs. Choi.

329
00:17:45,300 --> 00:17:47,570
Last night, Mi Mi...

330
00:17:47,670 --> 00:17:51,340
drank four glasses of soju.

331
00:17:51,410 --> 00:17:52,610
What?

332
00:17:52,680 --> 00:17:55,180
- Four glasses?
- Mom usually...

333
00:17:55,250 --> 00:17:56,980
passed out
after three glasses, right?

334
00:17:57,050 --> 00:18:00,380
Exactly. After Gang Nam's divorce,

335
00:18:00,450 --> 00:18:03,420
the shock must have made your mom
lose her mind.

336
00:18:05,760 --> 00:18:08,390
Do you know how much
life's pain and bitterness...

337
00:18:08,460 --> 00:18:11,860
can drastically increase
a person's alcohol tolerance?

338
00:18:11,930 --> 00:18:13,330
Do you?

339
00:18:13,400 --> 00:18:15,430
What are you saving
your employee discount for?

340
00:18:19,300 --> 00:18:21,610
(K Department Store)

341
00:18:24,480 --> 00:18:28,280
I want to give my sister-in-law
at least some money.

342
00:18:28,350 --> 00:18:30,980
But the scarf I like is expensive.

343
00:18:32,020 --> 00:18:33,580
(K Department Store)

344
00:18:34,590 --> 00:18:37,520
Gosh, why am I hesitating
at a time like this?

345
00:18:37,590 --> 00:18:39,360
Am I really Mom's daughter?

346
00:18:39,420 --> 00:18:42,030
Mom drank four glasses of soju.

347
00:18:46,330 --> 00:18:47,660
Oh, boy.

348
00:18:56,610 --> 00:18:59,110
- I am back.
- Okay.

349
00:18:59,180 --> 00:19:01,850
But which customer is this for?

350
00:19:01,910 --> 00:19:03,910
I do not think it was
on the reservation list.

351
00:19:03,980 --> 00:19:06,320
I am going to buy it.
As a gift for my mom.

352
00:19:08,850 --> 00:19:10,250
Even though it is expensive,

353
00:19:10,320 --> 00:19:12,260
it definitely catches
the eye the most.

354
00:19:12,320 --> 00:19:13,890
Right?

355
00:19:13,960 --> 00:19:16,190
Your mother will really love it.

356
00:19:16,260 --> 00:19:18,200
Shall I go ahead and pay?

357
00:19:30,310 --> 00:19:31,840
Welcome, sir.

358
00:19:33,480 --> 00:19:35,450
Did you make a reservation?

359
00:19:35,510 --> 00:19:36,510
No.

360
00:19:37,210 --> 00:19:38,350
(Song Min Hee)

361
00:19:38,420 --> 00:19:40,480
Are you looking for
anything in particular?

362
00:19:42,190 --> 00:19:44,220
I am looking for a women's scarf.

363
00:19:44,290 --> 00:19:47,930
May I ask the age group
of the woman you are buying it for?

364
00:19:50,830 --> 00:19:55,070
Get me a silk scarf
with small floral patterns.

365
00:19:55,970 --> 00:20:00,440
Your father, Jun Sung,
used to love it when I wore a scarf.

366
00:20:00,500 --> 00:20:03,770
He'd always say
how pretty his mom looked.

367
00:20:06,640 --> 00:20:07,640
Sir.

368
00:20:10,680 --> 00:20:11,820
It's for my girlfriend.

369
00:20:15,490 --> 00:20:16,490
I'll take this one.

370
00:20:19,090 --> 00:20:20,320
Well...

371
00:20:20,390 --> 00:20:21,830
Is there a problem?

372
00:20:22,830 --> 00:20:24,360
(K Department Store)

373
00:20:24,430 --> 00:20:26,230
Just a moment.

374
00:20:26,300 --> 00:20:29,030
- Yes.
- Manager Kang.

375
00:20:29,100 --> 00:20:32,700
That customer wants to buy the scarf
you picked out. What should I do?

376
00:20:37,240 --> 00:20:39,140
That's the guy
from the elevator yesterday.

377
00:20:42,450 --> 00:20:44,450
(K Department Store)

378
00:20:46,250 --> 00:20:48,220
Hello, sir.

379
00:20:48,290 --> 00:20:49,350
We meet again.

380
00:20:51,220 --> 00:20:52,960
Hello.

381
00:20:53,020 --> 00:20:54,630
You must work here.

382
00:20:54,690 --> 00:20:56,160
Yes.

383
00:20:56,230 --> 00:20:59,030
Are you feeling any better?

384
00:20:59,100 --> 00:21:02,670
Yes, I'm much better, thanks to you.
You helped me out a lot,

385
00:21:02,730 --> 00:21:05,570
but I was so out of it yesterday.

386
00:21:05,640 --> 00:21:08,610
I should at least
treat you to a meal.

387
00:21:08,670 --> 00:21:12,210
If you don't mind,
could I get your number?

388
00:21:15,010 --> 00:21:19,580
That might be difficult, sir.
Personal meetings with customers...

389
00:21:19,650 --> 00:21:22,550
are strictly prohibited
under our VIP service policy.

390
00:21:24,960 --> 00:21:27,990
Then how can I repay you
for your help?

391
00:21:29,830 --> 00:21:31,260
Actually,

392
00:21:31,330 --> 00:21:34,000
the item you selected...

393
00:21:34,060 --> 00:21:37,500
has already been paid for
by another customer.

394
00:21:37,570 --> 00:21:41,640
So we can't sell it to you.
I ask for your understanding.

395
00:21:41,710 --> 00:21:43,040
Would it be all right
if I recommended...

396
00:21:43,140 --> 00:21:44,340
some other items?

397
00:21:46,710 --> 00:21:48,750
It was exactly
what I was looking for,

398
00:21:48,810 --> 00:21:49,810
so that's a shame.

399
00:21:50,950 --> 00:21:51,980
But it can't be helped.

400
00:21:56,120 --> 00:21:57,790
Wait a minute.

401
00:21:57,850 --> 00:21:58,860
Yes?

402
00:22:01,360 --> 00:22:04,190
I seem to be the only customer
in this store right now.

403
00:22:04,260 --> 00:22:06,460
Who exactly just paid for it?

404
00:22:09,470 --> 00:22:10,930
Well, you see...

405
00:22:12,000 --> 00:22:14,570
I just want to know the truth.

406
00:22:14,670 --> 00:22:17,310
You can just give me
an honest answer, Manager.

407
00:22:18,840 --> 00:22:21,750
That other customer is actually...

408
00:22:23,210 --> 00:22:24,250
me.

409
00:22:25,950 --> 00:22:28,190
- What?
- According to our store policy,

410
00:22:28,250 --> 00:22:30,320
a customer's intent to purchase
takes priority...

411
00:22:30,390 --> 00:22:32,360
over an employee
buying at a discount.

412
00:22:32,420 --> 00:22:33,620
I am truly sorry.

413
00:22:34,790 --> 00:22:38,930
It's the first time I'm buying
an expensive gift for my mother,

414
00:22:39,000 --> 00:22:41,470
and I really wanted
to get it for her this one time.

415
00:22:44,330 --> 00:22:46,470
It was a gift for your mother?

416
00:22:46,540 --> 00:22:47,970
I am so sorry.

417
00:22:49,270 --> 00:22:53,010
But if you really want to
repay your gratitude to me,

418
00:22:53,040 --> 00:22:57,110
how about you be considerate
and let me buy that scarf?

419
00:22:58,820 --> 00:23:00,650
No, it is not a matter
of being considerate.

420
00:23:00,720 --> 00:23:02,820
Please give it
to your mother as a gift.

421
00:23:02,890 --> 00:23:04,920
Thank you so much.

422
00:23:04,990 --> 00:23:06,390
Then, another scarf...

423
00:23:06,460 --> 00:23:08,690
No, I am not interested
in other scarves.

424
00:23:08,760 --> 00:23:11,160
The only one that caught my eye
was that exact scarf.

425
00:23:12,800 --> 00:23:13,830
I see.

426
00:23:15,630 --> 00:23:17,200
By the way,

427
00:23:17,270 --> 00:23:19,540
is what you said earlier
actually true?

428
00:23:21,140 --> 00:23:22,370
What...

429
00:23:22,440 --> 00:23:24,440
That personal meetings
with customers...

430
00:23:24,510 --> 00:23:26,580
are prohibited
by the department store policy.

431
00:23:28,850 --> 00:23:31,010
While wearing our uniforms,

432
00:23:31,050 --> 00:23:33,980
meeting during work hours
for work-related matters...

433
00:23:35,050 --> 00:23:36,390
is, yes, allowed.

434
00:23:37,420 --> 00:23:39,790
I see. I understand for now.

435
00:23:39,860 --> 00:23:41,460
Kang Da Mi.

436
00:23:41,530 --> 00:23:44,800
I am sure your mother will love it.
Keep up the good work.

437
00:23:46,830 --> 00:23:47,900
Have a good day.

438
00:23:57,640 --> 00:23:59,480
How do you know him, Da Mi?

439
00:24:02,010 --> 00:24:03,010
Da Mi.

440
00:24:04,410 --> 00:24:07,280
Oh, we just bumped
into each other...

441
00:24:07,350 --> 00:24:08,950
From what I heard earlier,

442
00:24:09,020 --> 00:24:10,890
he said he was going
to give it to his girlfriend.

443
00:24:10,950 --> 00:24:14,160
He is a bit dry, but also cool.

444
00:24:14,220 --> 00:24:16,030
He said it is for his girlfriend?

445
00:24:16,090 --> 00:24:17,930
Yes.

446
00:24:17,990 --> 00:24:19,400
Now I feel even more sorry.

447
00:24:20,960 --> 00:24:23,130
But where have I seen him before?

448
00:24:23,200 --> 00:24:25,200
Even if I was too distracted
to notice yesterday,

449
00:24:25,270 --> 00:24:27,070
he is definitely a familiar face.

450
00:24:42,620 --> 00:24:44,890
Oh, my. I am sorry.

451
00:24:48,560 --> 00:24:49,560
Excuse me.

452
00:24:53,360 --> 00:24:54,660
What is wrong with her?

453
00:25:09,680 --> 00:25:10,950
Do you not see that?

454
00:25:11,010 --> 00:25:12,020
See what?

455
00:25:14,680 --> 00:25:17,520
Oh, my, was that yours?

456
00:25:17,590 --> 00:25:20,660
Is there anyone else here
besides you and me right now?

457
00:25:21,830 --> 00:25:23,790
If you bumped into my shoulder
and made me drop it,

458
00:25:23,860 --> 00:25:25,630
it is only polite
that you pick it up.

459
00:25:25,700 --> 00:25:28,400
Or at least pretend
to help me pick it up.

460
00:25:28,470 --> 00:25:29,470
Am I wrong?

461
00:25:31,330 --> 00:25:32,470
(Hwanggeum Group, Visitor No. 071)

462
00:25:33,740 --> 00:25:35,740
Is this your first time
at our company?

463
00:25:35,810 --> 00:25:37,270
No, it is not.

464
00:25:37,340 --> 00:25:38,910
Right.

465
00:25:38,980 --> 00:25:40,710
What do you mean, "Right?"

466
00:25:42,180 --> 00:25:45,550
Ma'am. Please pick those up for her.

467
00:25:46,880 --> 00:25:49,290
Happy now?
I am busy, so if you will excuse me.

468
00:25:54,220 --> 00:25:55,730
What a total lunatic.

469
00:26:00,830 --> 00:26:02,370
Leave it, ma'am, I will do it.

470
00:26:05,840 --> 00:26:10,710
Oh, my.
You are such a polite young lady.

471
00:26:10,770 --> 00:26:11,840
Thank you.

472
00:26:25,690 --> 00:26:27,620
Do you have an outside meeting,
Team Leader Cha?

473
00:26:27,690 --> 00:26:30,430
- No, my sister came to visit.
- Oh, right.

474
00:26:30,490 --> 00:26:32,130
You said you had
a younger sister, right?

475
00:26:32,200 --> 00:26:34,430
Yes, I will be away
for about 30 minutes.

476
00:26:37,030 --> 00:26:39,170
I have a question about something.

477
00:26:39,240 --> 00:26:40,340
It is not about work.

478
00:26:43,040 --> 00:26:44,510
Okay.

479
00:26:44,570 --> 00:26:46,010
Feel free to ask me anything.

480
00:26:47,380 --> 00:26:49,780
I mean women around your age,
Assistant Manager Kang.

481
00:26:52,420 --> 00:26:55,450
An acquaintance of mine
went to a department store,

482
00:26:55,520 --> 00:26:57,590
and while he was buying
a suit for himself,

483
00:26:57,650 --> 00:26:59,060
from the clothes
he was originally wearing,

484
00:26:59,120 --> 00:27:00,920
a woman's underwear fell out.

485
00:27:00,990 --> 00:27:03,530
Of all people, a female employee
at the store saw it happen.

486
00:27:03,530 --> 00:27:05,130
But the truth is...

487
00:27:05,200 --> 00:27:06,400
the underwear belonged
to my acquaintance's...

488
00:27:06,460 --> 00:27:08,930
- younger sister...
- Stop right there, Team Leader Cha.

489
00:27:09,000 --> 00:27:12,270
Excuse me?
He says he was falsely accused.

490
00:27:12,340 --> 00:27:13,940
There is more to the story.

491
00:27:14,000 --> 00:27:16,570
I do not need to hear any more,
Team Leader Cha.

492
00:27:16,640 --> 00:27:18,410
If you keep someone like that
as an acquaintance,

493
00:27:18,480 --> 00:27:21,950
it will do you a lot of harm.
Please cut ties with him.

494
00:27:22,010 --> 00:27:23,610
Why is that?

495
00:27:23,680 --> 00:27:26,020
He is 100 percent a pervert.

496
00:27:26,050 --> 00:27:28,180
If I were that
department store employee,

497
00:27:28,250 --> 00:27:29,620
I would have called
security immediately.

498
00:27:30,690 --> 00:27:33,090
I am giving you my sincere advice.

499
00:27:33,160 --> 00:27:36,130
Well, have a good time
with your sister.

500
00:27:43,700 --> 00:27:44,770
A pervert?

501
00:27:51,170 --> 00:27:53,240
Wow, Cha Se Na.

502
00:27:53,310 --> 00:27:57,380
You just wait.
Your pervert brother...

503
00:27:57,450 --> 00:27:58,920
is coming down right now.

504
00:28:06,420 --> 00:28:09,230
(Mission: Mompossible)

505
00:28:09,290 --> 00:28:10,830
Madam Chairwoman,

506
00:28:10,890 --> 00:28:13,560
do you think Seung Yun
figured something out...

507
00:28:13,560 --> 00:28:14,860
on his own and left?

508
00:28:14,860 --> 00:28:18,100
That boy left
to build up his strength.

509
00:28:18,100 --> 00:28:20,670
You have been through a lot, oh my.

510
00:28:20,740 --> 00:28:24,040
About what happened that day.
I am not a pervert.

511
00:28:25,140 --> 00:28:26,480
Dating is out of the question.

512
00:28:27,980 --> 00:28:29,980
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
